        "thought_text": "Derive a closed-form formula based on the property that the sum of a submatrix $b_{ij}$ for rows $x..y$ and columns $z..t$ equals $( ext{sum}(s[x..y])) imes ( ext{sum}(s[z..t]))$. The problem reduces to finding pairs of subarrays whose product equals $a$. This avoids $O(N^4)$ iteration.",
